      "hints": [
        "Identify the constant term in $\\left(2x + \\frac{k}{x}\\right)^6$: $\\binom{6}{3}(2x)^3\\left(\\frac{k}{x}\\right)^3 = 160k^3$.",
        "Equate $160k^3 = 540$ and solve for $k$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write down the general term in the binomial expansion of $\\left(2x + \\frac{k}{x}\\right)^6$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{6}{r}(2x)^{6-r}\\left(\\frac{k}{x}\\right)^r = \\binom{6}{r}2^{6-r}k^r x^{6-2r}$$",
        "Set the power of $x$ equal to zero ($6 - 2r = 0 \\implies r = 3$) to isolate the independent term:\n$$\\text{Constant term} = \\binom{6}{3}(2x)^3\\left(\\frac{k}{x}\\right)^3 = 20(8)k^3 = 160k^3$$",
        "Equate to $540$ and solve for $k$:\n$$160k^3 = 540 \\implies k^3 = \\frac{540}{160} = \\frac{27}{8} \\implies k = \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{27}{8}} = \\frac{3}{2} \\quad (\\text{or } 1.5)$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Binomial Expansion": "Identifies term $160k^3$ (B2). Solves $160k^3 = 540$ to obtain $k = \\frac{3}{2}$ (B1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
      }
