        "Substitute $k = \\frac{3}{2}$ to evaluate the coefficient."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set the power of $x$ equal to $2$ ($6 - 2r = 2 \\implies 2r = 4 \\implies r = 2$):\n$$\\text{Term in } x^2 = \\binom{6}{2}(2x)^4\\left(\\frac{k}{x}\\right)^2 = 15(16k^2)x^2 = 240k^2 x^2$$",
        "Substitute $k = \\frac{3}{2}$ into the coefficient expression:\n$$\\text{Coefficient} = 240\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2 = 240 \\times \\frac{9}{4} = 60 \\times 9 = 540$$"
